1. Scope and definitions

This license applies to the original source code, binaries, documentation,
and other material that a copyright holder expressly makes available under
this license (the "Covered Material"). A "Licensor" is a copyright holder,
or its authorized representative, granting rights that it is entitled to
grant in the Covered Material. "You" means the person or legal entity
exercising rights under this license.

Material identified as subject to a separate license, including third-party
libraries, fonts, tools, games, and IDEs, is not relicensed by this document.
Its own license continues to govern it. Merely distributing independent
third-party material alongside the Covered Material does not make that
third-party material subject to this license.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying the Covered
Material in the version You distribute, including Your modifications and
the build scripts, configuration, and language definitions needed to build
that covered version. It does not include private signing keys, passwords,
access tokens, or the source of independent third-party software. Identify
the versions and sources of required third-party dependencies and retain
any notices or source-offer obligations required by their own licenses.

2. Limited noncommercial permission

Subject to all conditions below, each Licensor grants You a nonexclusive,
worldwide, royalty-free permission to use, copy, study, and modify the
Covered Material for noncommercial purposes, and to distribute it for
noncommercial purposes without charging recipients, under section 4.

Personal learning, private entertainment, and hobby projects without a
commercial purpose are permitted. Private noncommercial modifications do
not have to be published. There is no automatic exemption for an
organization based on its legal form, funding, or public-interest status.

3. Commercial use and sales require separate written permission

The permission in section 2 does not cover an activity with a commercial
purpose, whether that purpose is primary or secondary, including commercial
advantage, commercial revenue generation, or the operation of a business.
Before undertaking such an activity involving the Covered
Material, You must obtain a separate written license from every relevant
Licensor, or a representative authorized to grant the necessary rights.

Without that permission, You may not:

(a) sell, rent, license for a fee, or charge for access to the Covered
    Material, a modified version, or a product or modpack containing it;
(b) use the Covered Material to provide paid hosting, paid game servers,
    subscription features, managed services, or other paid services;
(c) use the Covered Material as part of an activity monetized through
    advertising, commercial sponsorship, or other commercial means; or
(d) deploy or use the Covered Material for the internal operation of a
    commercial business.

Offering the software itself for free does not make an otherwise
commercial activity noncommercial. This section does not prohibit personal
learning merely because the skills acquired might later be useful at work.

A separate written license may authorize specified commercial uses or
different distribution terms. It overrides this license only to the extent
expressly agreed and only for rights the granting party is entitled to
license. No contributor's copyright is assigned or made available for
commercial relicensing merely by contributing or distributing changes.

4. Conditions for noncommercial redistribution

For every copy of Covered Material You distribute, whether modified or
unmodified, You must:

(a) provide this complete license and retain applicable copyright,
    attribution, and third-party notices;
(b) clearly identify Your modifications and their dates, and avoid
    presenting a modified version as an official release;
(c) provide the Corresponding Source with the copy, or provide a working
    link allowing recipients to download that exact Corresponding Source
    at no charge, without requiring a separate agreement or credentials;
    the link must remain available for at least three years after Your
    last distribution of that version;
(d) distribute Your modifications to the Covered Material under this same
    license, unless all relevant rights holders have separately authorized
    another license; and
(e) impose no additional terms that prevent recipients from exercising
    the noncommercial rights granted by this license.

Publishing only an unrelated version or a link to a changing development
branch is not sufficient to provide the Corresponding Source of a binary.
This section is triggered by distribution; it does not itself require the
publication of private changes used without distribution. Commercial
network services remain subject to section 3.

